{
	"info": {
		"_postman_id": "fdp-notification-service-collection",
		"name": "FDP - notification-service (MongoDB + async events demo)",
		"description": "notification-service has no write API of its own -- it only consumes order-service's RabbitMQ events (RULES.md §6) and records them in MongoDB (`notification_db`, RULES.md §5). This collection places (and cancels) a real order through order-service to generate real `OrderPlacedEvent`/`OrderCancelledEvent` messages, then reads the resulting notifications back through notification-service's own REST API. Requires `customer-service` (:8082), `restaurant-service` (:8083), `order-service` (:8084), `notification-service` (:8086), `discovery-server` (:8761), and `config-server` (:8888) all running -- see RUNNING.md. Import the sibling `FDP.postman_environment.json` and select it before running.\n\nRun order: **1. Get Tokens**, then **2. Prerequisite Setup** (self-contained -- registers its own customer/address/restaurant/menu item so this collection doesn't depend on the other collections having run first), then **3. Trigger Events via Order Placement**, then **4. Read Notifications**, then **5. Negative / Security Tests**.\n\nA small delay is built into the run (Newman: pass `--delay-request 800` for extra margin) because event consumption is asynchronous -- the notification typically lands in MongoDB within a couple hundred milliseconds of the order-service request returning, but it is never simultaneous with it.\n\nTo see the idempotency guard for yourself: check RabbitMQ's management UI (http://localhost:15672, login fdp/fdp) -- `notification-service.order-events` is bound to `fdp.order-events` with pattern `order.#`; publishing the exact same message twice (matching `eventId`) produces only one notification record, because `NotificationRecord.eventId` carries a unique index and a losing concurrent write is caught and ignored, not just short-circuited by an application-level check.",
		"schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
	},
	"item": [
		{
			"name": "1. Get Tokens (Keycloak)",
			"item": [
				{
					"name": "Get Customer Token",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"const body = pm.response.json();",
									"pm.test('token issued', () => pm.expect(body.access_token).to.be.a('string'));",
									"pm.environment.set('customerToken', body.access_token);"
								]
							}
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/x-www-form-urlencoded" }],
						"body": {
							"mode": "urlencoded",
							"urlencoded": [
								{ "key": "grant_type", "value": "password" },
								{ "key": "client_id", "value": "{{clientId}}" },
								{ "key": "username", "value": "{{customerUsername}}" },
								{ "key": "password", "value": "{{customerPassword}}" }
							]
						},
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{keycloakUrl}}/realms/{{realm}}/protocol/openid-connect/token",
							"host": ["{{keycloakUrl}}"],
							"path": ["realms", "{{realm}}", "protocol", "openid-connect", "token"]
						}
					}
				},
				{
					"name": "Get Restaurant Owner Token",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"const body = pm.response.json();",
									"pm.test('token issued', () => pm.expect(body.access_token).to.be.a('string'));",
									"pm.environment.set('restaurantOwnerToken', body.access_token);"
								]
							}
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/x-www-form-urlencoded" }],
						"body": {
							"mode": "urlencoded",
							"urlencoded": [
								{ "key": "grant_type", "value": "password" },
								{ "key": "client_id", "value": "{{clientId}}" },
								{ "key": "username", "value": "{{restaurantOwnerUsername}}" },
								{ "key": "password", "value": "{{restaurantOwnerPassword}}" }
							]
						},
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{keycloakUrl}}/realms/{{realm}}/protocol/openid-connect/token",
							"host": ["{{keycloakUrl}}"],
							"path": ["realms", "{{realm}}", "protocol", "openid-connect", "token"]
						}
					}
				},
				{
					"name": "Get Admin Token",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"const body = pm.response.json();",
									"pm.test('token issued', () => pm.expect(body.access_token).to.be.a('string'));",
									"pm.environment.set('adminToken', body.access_token);"
								]
							}
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/x-www-form-urlencoded" }],
						"body": {
							"mode": "urlencoded",
							"urlencoded": [
								{ "key": "grant_type", "value": "password" },
								{ "key": "client_id", "value": "{{clientId}}" },
								{ "key": "username", "value": "{{adminUsername}}" },
								{ "key": "password", "value": "{{adminPassword}}" }
							]
						},
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{keycloakUrl}}/realms/{{realm}}/protocol/openid-connect/token",
							"host": ["{{keycloakUrl}}"],
							"path": ["realms", "{{realm}}", "protocol", "openid-connect", "token"]
						}
					}
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"name": "2. Prerequisite Setup (self-contained)",
			"description": "Registers everything an order needs to reference: a customer profile + address (customer-service) and a restaurant + menu item (restaurant-service). Safe to skip if you already ran the other collections against a fresh database -- just make sure addressId/restaurantId/menuItemId are populated in the environment.",
			"item": [
				{
					"name": "Register Customer Profile",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": ["pm.test('created or already exists', () => [200,201,409].includes(pm.response.code));"] }
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [
							{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{customerToken}}" },
							{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
						],
						"body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"phoneNumber\": \"+15551234567\"\n}", "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } } },
						"url": { "raw": "{{customerServiceUrl}}/api/customers/me", "host": ["{{customerServiceUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "customers", "me"] }
					}
				},
				{
					"name": "Add Delivery Address",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test('created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
									"pm.environment.set('addressId', pm.response.json().id);"
								]
							}
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [
							{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{customerToken}}" },
							{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
						],
						"body": {
							"mode": "raw",
							"raw": "{\n  \"label\": \"Home\",\n  \"street\": \"12 Kigali Ave\",\n  \"city\": \"Kigali\",\n  \"state\": \"Kigali City\",\n  \"postalCode\": \"00000\",\n  \"country\": \"Rwanda\",\n  \"isDefault\": true\n}",
							"options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
						},
						"url": { "raw": "{{customerServiceUrl}}/api/customers/me/addresses", "host": ["{{customerServiceUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "customers", "me", "addresses"] }
					}
				},
				{
					"name": "Register Restaurant",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": ["pm.test('created or already exists', () => [200,201,409].includes(pm.response.code));", "if (pm.response.code === 201) { pm.environment.set('restaurantId', pm.response.json().id); }"] }
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [
							{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{restaurantOwnerToken}}" },
							{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
						],
						"body": {
							"mode": "raw",
							"raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Kigali Grill\",\n  \"description\": \"Grilled specialties\",\n  \"cuisineType\": \"Rwandan\",\n  \"street\": \"1 Downtown Ave\",\n  \"city\": \"Kigali\",\n  \"state\": \"Kigali City\",\n  \"postalCode\": \"00000\",\n  \"country\": \"Rwanda\"\n}",
							"options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
						},
						"url": { "raw": "{{restaurantServiceUrl}}/api/restaurants/me", "host": ["{{restaurantServiceUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "restaurants", "me"] }
					}
				},
				{
					"name": "Get My Restaurant (fills restaurantId if it already existed)",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": ["pm.test('ok', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));", "pm.environment.set('restaurantId', pm.response.json().id);"] }
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"method": "GET",
						"header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{restaurantOwnerToken}}" }],
						"url": { "raw": "{{restaurantServiceUrl}}/api/restaurants/me", "host": ["{{restaurantServiceUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "restaurants", "me"] }
					}
				},
				{
					"name": "Add Menu Item",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test('created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
									"pm.environment.set('menuItemId', pm.response.json().id);"
								]
							}
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [
							{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{restaurantOwnerToken}}" },
							{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
						],
						"body": {
							"mode": "raw",
							"raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Brochette\",\n  \"description\": \"Grilled skewers\",\n  \"price\": 5.50,\n  \"category\": \"Mains\",\n  \"available\": true\n}",
							"options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
						},
						"url": { "raw": "{{restaurantServiceUrl}}/api/restaurants/me/menu-items", "host": ["{{restaurantServiceUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "restaurants", "me", "menu-items"] }
					}
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"name": "3. Trigger Events via Order Placement",
			"description": "notification-service never sees these requests -- they go straight to order-service. Placing/cancelling an order publishes OrderPlacedEvent/OrderCancelledEvent onto fdp.order-events, which notification-service consumes independently (RULES.md §6). Included here (rather than assuming the order-service collection already ran) so this collection is self-contained end to end.",
			"item": [
				{
					"name": "Place Order (publishes OrderPlacedEvent)",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test('created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
									"const body = pm.response.json();",
									"pm.test('status is PLACED', () => pm.expect(body.status).to.eql('PLACED'));",
									"pm.environment.set('orderId', body.id);"
								]
							}
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [
							{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{customerToken}}" },
							{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
						],
						"body": {
							"mode": "raw",
							"raw": "{\n  \"restaurantId\": {{restaurantId}},\n  \"deliveryAddressId\": {{addressId}},\n  \"items\": [\n    {\"menuItemId\": {{menuItemId}}, \"quantity\": 2}\n  ]\n}",
							"options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
						},
						"url": { "raw": "{{orderServiceUrl}}/api/orders/me", "host": ["{{orderServiceUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "orders", "me"] }
					}
				},
				{
					"name": "Cancel Order (publishes OrderCancelledEvent)",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": ["pm.test('ok', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));", "pm.test('now cancelled', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().status).to.eql('CANCELLED'));"] }
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{customerToken}}" }],
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{orderServiceUrl}}/api/orders/me/{{orderId}}/cancel",
							"host": ["{{orderServiceUrl}}"],
							"path": ["api", "orders", "me", "{{orderId}}", "cancel"]
						}
					}
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"name": "4. Read Notifications",
			"item": [
				{
					"name": "My Notifications (self-service, authenticated only)",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"type": "text/javascript",
								"exec": [
									"pm.test('ok', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
									"const body = pm.response.json();",
									"pm.test('paged shape', () => pm.expect(body).to.have.property('content'));",
									"pm.test('at least one ORDER_PLACED and one ORDER_CANCELLED recorded', () => {",
									"  const types = body.content.map(n => n.eventType);",
									"  pm.expect(types).to.include('ORDER_PLACED');",
									"  pm.expect(types).to.include('ORDER_CANCELLED');",
									"});"
								]
							}
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"method": "GET",
						"header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{customerToken}}" }],
						"url": { "raw": "{{notificationServiceUrl}}/api/notifications/me", "host": ["{{notificationServiceUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "notifications", "me"] }
					}
				},
				{
					"name": "All Notifications (admin only)",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": ["pm.test('ok', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));", "pm.test('paged shape', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json()).to.have.property('content'));"] }
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"method": "GET",
						"header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{adminToken}}" }],
						"url": { "raw": "{{notificationServiceUrl}}/api/notifications", "host": ["{{notificationServiceUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "notifications"] }
					}
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"name": "5. Negative / Security Tests",
			"item": [
				{
					"name": "No Token -> 401",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": ["pm.test('unauthorized', () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));"] }
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"method": "GET",
						"header": [],
						"url": { "raw": "{{notificationServiceUrl}}/api/notifications/me", "host": ["{{notificationServiceUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "notifications", "me"] }
					}
				},
				{
					"name": "Plain Customer Cannot List All -> 403",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": ["pm.test('forbidden -- lacks notification:read', () => pm.response.to.have.status(403));"] }
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"method": "GET",
						"header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{customerToken}}" }],
						"url": { "raw": "{{notificationServiceUrl}}/api/notifications", "host": ["{{notificationServiceUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "notifications"] },
						"description": "customer@fdp.test's role set doesn't include notification:read -- only ADMIN carries that permission (docker/keycloak/fdp-realm.json)."
					}
				}
			]
		}
	]
}
